  "count": 2,
  "rationale": "Deploying mfa:admin and mfa:dbadmin together blocks every exfiltration path. mfa:admin blocks auth_dc and auth_adfs, so admin_dc and admin_adfs can never be reached. With mfa:dbadmin also deployed, auth_db, auth_fileserver and auth_backup each need admin_dc or admin_adfs, which are now unreachable. No db, fileserver or backup foothold is possible, so exfiltration cannot happen. No single control is enough. Segmented alone fails because phishing plus escalate_workstation gives admin_workstation, which bypasses segmentation. mfa:user is bypassed because phishing gives a workstation foothold. mfa:admin alone fails because stolen_dbadmin can still come from the ciserver secret leak (kerberoast gives stolen_admin, then escalate_ciserver). mfa:dbadmin alone fails because auth_dc and escalate_dc give admin_dc. Patching the ciserver, appserver or apiserver is bypassed by stolen_admin. Perimeter patches are bypassed by phishing. patched_dc, patched_adfs, patched_db, patched_fileserver and patched_backup appear in no technique's requirements, so they block nothing. The minimum is therefore 2."
